Practical philosophy notes: toward a trial text for critical readers
    : re `critical readers` viz. `senior students` @ 01.lynchpin/00.lynchpin.brec

    premise+ how the default ground entails|{would entail} our carrying on
        - already this would allow me (given how difficult ground knowledge is likely to prove)
          to suggest that here we begin to see a strange coincidence between (1) and (2)
        + work backwards to this premise (and/or its likes), beginning from the minimum (of conditions)
          that would suffice to justify belief in a design explanans
            / ∵ working forward has proven as feasible as pushing spaghetti
        ? what minimum (of coincidence) would (surprise enough to) call for explanation?
            • (the coincidence of) direction by [practical] reason/logic to (the end of) carrying on
              in a manner (surprise!) well supported by the safehold
                • direction by [practical] reason/logic to (the end of) carrying on
                  [for] an open-ended and likely long period [of time]
                    • that period being, in our present prospect|outlook,
                      necessarily uncertain and ∴ {open-ended}|inderminate
                        • we know (at present) of no method to [reliably]
                          bound|{predict|determine a [upper] bound|limit on}
                          {how long}|{the period|{length of time}} [it would take]
                          to acquire ground knowledge
                    • that period being unlikely (relative to the length of past efforts) to be short
                        • long {[have] we tried}|{did we try} [in [the] past] to acquire ground knowledge
                          and its likes and {in the end}|ultimately {[we] failed}|{did [we] fail}
                            • ∃ [at present] no settled consensus on the ground question or its likes
